Meta description: Get up to ₹78,000 subsidy for rooftop solar in West Bengal under PM Surya Ghar. Check eligibility, subsidy amount, DCR rules and the step-by-step application process.

Last updated: October 2026
Rooftop solar is becoming a practical way for households in West Bengal to cut their electricity bills. The PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana is a Government of India scheme that gives eligible homes a direct subsidy for installing a rooftop solar system.
This guide explains how much subsidy you can get, who is eligible, and how to apply.
How much subsidy can you receive?
The central subsidy is ₹30,000 per kW for the first 2 kW, and ₹18,000 for the 3rd kW. The maximum is ₹78,000.
Solar system capacity	Central subsidy
1 kW	₹30,000
2 kW	₹60,000
3 kW or above	₹78,000 (maximum)

The subsidy does not increase beyond 3 kW. A 5 kW or 10 kW home system still receives a maximum of ₹78,000.
Who is eligible?
•	The household must be in India and own a house with a roof suitable for solar panels.
•	The household must have a valid residential electricity connection from its DISCOM (WBSEDCL or CESC in West Bengal).
•	The household must not have already taken any other subsidy for rooftop solar.
•	The system must be installed by a registered vendor using DCR solar panels.
DCR panels are mandatory for the subsidy. Only rooftop systems built with DCR (Domestic Content Requirement) solar panels, made with Indian-manufactured cells, qualify for the PM Surya Ghar central subsidy. If non-DCR panels are installed, the full subsidy can be lost — so always ask your installer for the DCR certificate.
Application process: step by step
1.	Register on the national portal (pmsuryaghar.gov.in) with your state, electricity distribution company, consumer number, mobile number and email.
2.	Apply for rooftop solar through the portal.
3.	Get feasibility approval from your DISCOM.
4.	Choose a registered vendor and get the system installed.
5.	Submit the installation details on the portal and apply for a net meter.
6.	DISCOM inspection: after the net meter is installed and inspected, a commissioning certificate is generated.
7.	Submit your bank details and a cancelled cheque on the portal.
8.	Receive the subsidy directly in your bank account.
Always check the latest rules on the official portal: pmsuryaghar.gov.in.
Before you choose a vendor
Don't choose only on the advertised price. Compare the panel brand and DCR certificate, inverter quality, warranty, installation standards and after-sales support.
