Last updated: October 2026
One of the most common questions homeowners ask is whether to install a 3 kW or a 5 kW solar system. The answer depends mainly on how much electricity you use, not on the size of your house.
A 3 kW system may suit you if:
•	Your household electricity use is moderate
•	Roof space is limited
•	A good part of your electricity is used during the day
•	You want to get the full subsidy at the lowest system size
A 5 kW system may suit you if:
•	Your electricity use is considerably higher
•	You run multiple air conditioners
•	You use electric water heaters or pumps
•	You need more daytime generation
•	You have enough shadow-free roof area
Don't choose capacity based only on the subsidy
The PM Surya Ghar central subsidy reaches its maximum of ₹78,000 at 3 kW. A 5 kW system gets the same ₹78,000, not more. So the right question is: how much electricity does my household actually use?
Check your electricity bills for the last 6 to 12 months, including summer months, before deciding.
Quick comparison
Point	3 kW	5 kW
Suitable for	Moderate electricity use	High electricity use
Roof space needed	Less	More
Central subsidy	₹78,000	₹78,000 (same cap)
Upfront cost	Lower	Higher

Whatever the size, the panels must be DCR panels for the subsidy to apply.
