Rooftop solar can turn unused roof space into a source of clean electricity. For homeowners in Kolkata and across West Bengal, whether solar works for you depends on roof area, shading, electricity use and your grid connection.
Before installing solar, check these five things
1.	Electricity consumption: look at your recent electricity bills.
2.	Roof area: the available area decides how many panels can be installed.
3.	Shading: trees, neighbouring buildings and water tanks can reduce generation.
4.	Roof condition: the roof must be strong enough for the mounting structure.
5.	Electricity connection and DISCOM: grid-connected systems must follow your DISCOM's process.
Which DISCOM serves your area?
West Bengal has more than one electricity distribution company. Much of Kolkata and some nearby areas are supplied by CESC, while most of the rest of the state is served by WBSEDCL. The application, feasibility and net-metering steps go through whichever company supplies your home, so check your electricity bill to confirm.
Is solar suitable for every house?
Not always. A heavily shaded roof needs a different approach from a south-facing, open roof. That is why a proper site survey matters before you buy.
Subsidy for homeowners
Eligible residential customers can get central subsidy under PM Surya Ghar: up to ₹78,000 for a system of 3 kW or above. The system must use DCR panels and be installed by a registered vendor.
