Solar pumping for agriculture
A solar pumping system uses electricity from solar panels to run a water pump. It works especially well on farms where daytime irrigation is practical.
Solar and irrigation together
A farmer can combine:
Solar panels → Solar pump → Water storage / distribution → Drip or sprinkler irrigation
Solar pumping takes care of the energy needed to move water. Drip or sprinkler irrigation takes care of using that water efficiently. Together, they give better control over both water and energy.
Government schemes that can help
•	PM-KUSUM: support for standalone solar pumps and for solarising existing grid-connected pumps.
•	PMKSY – Per Drop More Crop: subsidy for drip and sprinkler irrigation.
•	MIDH: support for protected cultivation such as polyhouses.
Scheme rules and subsidy shares change, so check the current status for your district before investing.
